00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="9">
<![CDATA['L_TaskMon']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Label" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Label for graphic symbol displayed on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>0C 00 00 00 54 61 73 6B 20 4D 6F 6E 69 74 6F 72 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="12">
<![CDATA['Task Monitor']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Desc" DataType="STRING_40" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Description for display on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>12 00 00 00 4C 6F 67 69 78 20 54 61 73 6B 20 4D 
6F 6E 69 74 6F 72 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="18">
<![CDATA['Logix Task Monitor']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Lib" DataType="STRING_12" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Display Library for Faceplate call-up]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>06 00 00 00 52 41 2D 42 41 53 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="6">
<![CDATA['RA-BAS']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Monitor the Task containing this AOI and alarm if over planned scan time.]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
L_TaskMon:  LOGIX -- TASK MONITOR
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib, using P_Alarm V3.0.
V3.0-01  2013-07-30:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm V3.1.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction monitors the controller Task in which it is contained
and provides:

*  Display Values for Task configuration: Task Name, Priority, Rate, Watchdog settings
*  Display Values for Task statistics: Last and Max Execution time, Overlap Count
*  Display of the Task Inhibit / Active Status
*  Configuration of a "Plan" Execution Time, the time in which the Task is expected
 to always complete (including interrupts by higher priority Tasks)
*  An optional Alarm when Last (actual) Execution Time exceeds Plan
*  A Reset command, which clears and acknowledges the Over Plan Alarm.
*  Maintenance Commands to clear the Max Execution Time and Overlap Count.
*  A configurable single-letter Task Identifier (for HMI)
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION
============================================================
These rungs get Configuration data (such as alarm thresholds) and distribute
as needed.  Note that some Configuration data are used directly in-place.

Enter the PLAN (expected) execution time of the Task in MICROSECONDS.
If the actual execution time of the Task (which includes interrupts by higher priority
Tasks) exceeds this threshold, the OverPlan Status is raised
(and the OverPlan Alarm is raised if so configured).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)[GRT(Cfg_PlanExecT,20000.0) ,LES(Cfg_PlanExecT,0.0) ]OTE(Err_Plan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the reports of all Bad Configuration Status.
Individual bits are provided for various status:
Bad timer presets are determined in the Configuration logic above.
Bad Alarm configuration is determined by the P_Alarm instruction.

Then a summary Bad Config status is provided, simply an OR of the individual bits.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Err_Plan) ,XIC(OverPlan.Sts_Err) OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Commands and Input.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTL(OverPlan.Alm) ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ]OTL(OverPlan.PCmd_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the Clear Maximum Task Execution Time Maintenance Command.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_ClearMaxExecT)OTU(MCmd_ClearMaxExecT)[CLR(Wrk_MaxExecT) ,SSV(Task,This,MaxScanTime,Wrk_MaxExecT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the Clear Task Overlap Count Maintenance Command.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_ClearOverlapC)OTU(MCmd_ClearOverlapC)[CLR(Val_OverlapC) ,SSV(Task,This,OverlapCount,Val_OverlapC) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONTROLLER TASK MONITORING
============================================================
The following rungs monitor a controller Task and
provide data for the HMI and an Alarm for any Task that
is running longer than its expected time.

This rung provides the following Task configuration data:
* Task Inhibited status
* Task Name
* Task Priority
* Task Period (Rate) (ms)
* Task Watchdog Timeout setting (ms)

... and provides the following Task statistics:
* Task Last Execution Time (ms)
* Task Maximum Execution Time (ms)
* Task Overlap Count

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GSV(Task,THIS,InhibitTask,Wrk_Inhibited) NEQ(Wrk_Inhibited,0) OTE(Sts_TaskInhibited) ,GSV(Task,THIS,Name,Val_Name) GSV(Task,THIS,Priority,Val_Priority) ,GSV(Task,THIS,Rate,Wrk_Rate) MUL(Wrk_Rate,0.001,Val_Rate) ,GSV(Task,THIS,Watchdog,Wrk_WatchdogT) MUL(Wrk_WatchdogT,0.001,Val_WatchdogT) ,GSV(Task,THIS,LastScanTime,Wrk_LastExecT) MUL(Wrk_LastExecT,0.001,Val_LastExecT) ,GSV(Task,THIS,MaxScanTime,Wrk_MaxExecT) MUL(Wrk_MaxExecT,0.001,Val_MaxExecT) ,GSV(Task,THIS,OverlapCount,Val_OverlapC) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OVER PLAN STATUS
============================================================
If the Task is NOT inhibited, and if the Task Planned Execution Time
Configuration is valid, check to see if the Last Task Execution Time
exceeded the Plan value.  If so, set a status.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Sts_TaskInhibited)XIO(Err_Plan)GRT(Val_LastExecT,Cfg_PlanExecT)OTE(Sts_OverPlan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(OverPlan.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Task Time Over Plan alarm is ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTL(OverPlan.PCfg_AllowExist);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Task Time Over Plan Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(OverPlan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OverPlan.Sts_AlmInh)OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(OverPlan.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(OverPlan.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,XIC(OverPlan.Val_Notify.0) OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OverPlan.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(OverPlan.Rdy_Reset) OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
